{"text": "\u2014\u2014 Susan Z. Cohen\n\nEE \u2014_\u2014__ President\n=\u2014\u2014\u2014 Martin A. Goetz, MS, MPA\n> ah Chief Executive Ofer\n\u2014__\n\nBetty S. Sorna, CPA, MAcc\n\nChief Financial Officer\nRi EN | He rew Ho mM a Mauri Mizrahi, PT, GCS, LNHA\nAssociate Administrator\n\nSENIOR SERVICES | Wolfson Health & Aging Center aeub bles\n\nApril 14, 2020\n\nRon DeSantis, Governor, State of Florida\nPlaza Level 05, The Capitol\n400 S. Monroe Street\nTallahassee, FL 32399-0001\nEmail: GovernorRon.Desantis@eog.myflorida.com\n\nMary Mayhew, Secretary\nAgency for Health Care Administration\n2727 Mahan Drive, Mail Stop 1\nTallahassee, FL 32308\n\nEmail: mary.mayhew@ahca.myflorida.com\n\nScott A. Rivkees, MD, State Surgeon General\nSecretary, Florida Department of Health\n4052 Bald Cypress Way, Bin #A00\nTallahassee, FL 32399\nEmail: floridasurgeongeneral@flhealth.gov\n\nDear Governor DeSantis, Secretary Mayhew and Surgeon General Rivkees,\n\nThank you for implementing \u201cstrike teams\u201d using the Florida National Guard to implement\ntesting for COVID-19. What is now required is not assessments; it is testing \u2014 the immediate\ntesting of all residents and staff residing in nursing homes and ALFs. Not testing this most at-risk\npopulation, all of whom live in close quarters, is simply unconscionable.\n\nIt is well understood that COVID-19 is particularly deadly for older people \u2014 more so for seniors\nwho are already medically compromised. It is no accident that when COVID-19 enters a nursing\nfacility, the mortality rate can easily approach 50 percent. It is also well established that as many\nas 25 percent of individuals who are positive for the virus are asymptomatic, an especially\ntroubling statistic.\n\nWe demand testing immediately, starting with those nursing homes and ALFs throughout Florida\nthat have already been identified as having COVID-19 in their facilities and quickly expanding\nto everyone. This is an urgent need requiring an immediate response; anything short of an\nimmediate testing program places residents and staff in \u201cimmediate jeopardy.\u201d Telling facilities\nthat testing will begin in another week is unacceptable. The need is immediate and response must\nbe in proportion to the identified threat.\n\n11401 Old St. Augustine Road, Jacksonville, Florida 32258-1402 (904) 260-1818 Fax: (904) 260-9733 www.rivergarden.org\n\nFounded 1946 by the Lodies Hebrew Sheltering Aid Society * Sidney Entman 1911-1981 Founding Executive Director * A Beneficiary Agency ofthe Jewish Federation & Foundation of\nNortheast Florida * Nursing Care Center Accreditation and Post-Acute Certification by the Joint Commission",
